From f4e65592d765c216ae34e912fbc13c0bcff3eb8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:50:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] server: prompt tokens restored from kept states are
 counted in /metrics and /health; /v1/models names max_model_len

/metrics had only tensorfold:prompt_tokens_total, which counts cached and computed prompt tokens alike, so a dashboard
could not tell a 90%-cached agent workload from a computed one, and the per-request usage.prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens
was the only place the split showed. Metrics now also counts the tokens each finished request restored from a kept prompt
state (the mailbox's prefilled count): tensorfold:prompt_tokens_cached_total, repeated as vLLM's prefix_cache_hits_total
with prefix_cache_queries_total (= prompt tokens), and /health carries prompt_tokens_total, cached_tokens_total (the name
sparkDash reads) and generation_tokens_total, read together under the metrics lock so /health and /metrics agree.
Engine Info.prompt_cache says the engine keeps prompt states (set by the CUDA lane host when it has a cache); an engine
that keeps none publishes no cached counts. /v1/models entries gain max_model_len (the context window one request may
use) when the engine reports one.

Host tests (zig/tests/server/zig_test.sh, 85 tests): the counters in render and in /metrics and /health through a
request, absent without a cache, max_model_len present and absent.

Adapted from the 4x recipe's 0033 (manuel1618's pull request there, a backport of BertholomusAI's ce0d9053), plus /health
and /v1/models, which that patch does not touch.
